                                sling:resourceType="ajila-forms-customers/ajila-forms-ubs/components/controls/textdraw"
                                _value="&lt;p>Insurance coverage is provided in each case under the General Insurance Terms and Conditions (GCI) issued by the insurance company. The GCls and more information can be found at &lt;a title=&quot;www.ubs.com/reiseschutzplus&quot; href=&quot;http://www.ubs.com/reiseschutzplus&quot; data-clickable-id=&quot;clickable-4&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;>www.ubs.com/reiseschutzplus&lt;/a>. The annual card fee of CHF 98 is charged directly to the credit card account (in addition to annual card fee of UBS main card). UBS Travel Insurance Plus includes the following insurance components: cancellation, flight delay, luggage, purchase protection, foreign treatment costs, medical assistance, alternative travel and travel curtailment. The main card holder, persons living in the same household and underaged children who do not live in the same household are considered insured persons. The insurer is Europ Assistance (Switzerland) Insurances SA, Avenue Perdtemps 23, 1260 Nyon.&lt;br>&#xa;&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>UBS receives monetary benefits from Europ Assistance Versicherungen AG (&amp;quot;Europ Assistance&amp;quot;) for the referral of UBS cardholders to the UBS Travel Assistance Plus collective insurance contract between UBS and Europ Assistance (&amp;quot;insurance contract&amp;quot;). In particular, UBS advertises the insurance contract to appropriate UBS clients and executes administrative tasks (e.g. administration of contracts, collection of premiums, communication, statistics etc.). The personnel, IT and other costs for these tasks are paid out of the monetary benefits. Monetary benefits may lead to conflicts of interests on the part of UBS. They may in particular create incentives for UBS to refer the insurance contract with Europ Assistance over other contracts paying no, or less, monetary benefits. UBS has appropriate organizational measures in place in order to mitigate the risks resulting from such conflict of interests. UBS receives a maximum share of 24-33% of the cardholder's total annual insurance contract premium as monetary benefits. &lt;b>The cardholder agrees that UBS fully retains any monetary benefits received from Europ Assistance and herewith expressly waives the respective right to receive any monetary benefits. The cardholder acknowledges that this arrangement deviates from the statutory right to claim for restitution according to art. 400 para. 1 of the Swiss Code of Obligations or any other statutory provision with similar content.&lt;/b>&lt;/p>&#xa;"
